\section{Experiments and Results}
\label{sec:experiments}

We design our empirical evaluation to address four central questions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Void Trap Escape}: Does Single-Network DP-TS overcome the epistemic void collapse that paralyzes conventional BNNs on rugged multimodal landscapes?
    \item \textbf{High-Dimensional Policy Search}: Does DP-TS scale to high-dimensional continuous control ($d=32$) and robotics ($d=60$) where stationary GPs degrade?
    \item \textbf{Single-Network Superiority}: How does Single-Network DP-TS compare against parameter-space ensembles (multi-head LCB) and MC-Dropout?
    \item \textbf{Computational Scalability \& Latency}: Does DP-TS maintain fast, linear-time inference without matrix inversion bottlenecks?
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Experimental Setup and Baselines}
We benchmark Single-Network DP-TS against four primary methodologies:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Random Search}: Pure uniform random exploration across the search domain $\mathcal{X}$.
    \item \textbf{Standard BNN (MC-Dropout)} \citep{gal2016dropout}: 2-layer MLP (hidden dimension 64, SiLU activations) with dropout rate $p=0.2$, using $S=20$ stochastic forward passes for epistemic variance estimation under LCB ($\beta=2.2$).
    \item \textbf{Exact Gaussian Process (GP-BO)} \citep{rasmussen2006gaussian}: Exact GP regression with squared exponential / Mat\'ern kernel, lengthscale $\ell=\sqrt{d}$, and observation noise $\sigma_\epsilon^2 = 10^{-4}$ under LCB ($\beta=2.2$).
    \item \textbf{DP-BO (Multi-Head LCB)}: Parameter-space ensemble of $K=4$ neural heads trained on Dirichlet posterior draws with non-parametric support blending under LCB ($\beta=2.2$).
    \item \textbf{Single-Network DP-TS (Ours)}: A \textbf{single} deterministic 2-layer MLP ($K=1$) trained on freshly sampled Dirichlet posterior measures $\mathcal{P}_t$, executing pure Thompson Sampling without any $\beta$ hyperparameter.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Multimodal 2D Landscapes: Escaping Deceptive Local Traps}
We evaluate on two canonical multimodal benchmarks designed to stress-test local trap escape:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Ackley 2D}: Characterized by a flat outer plateau with concentric local ripples and a steep central basin at $(0, 0)$ with $f(0, 0)=0$. Initialized exclusively in the suboptimal quadrant $[3.0, 4.5]^2$ ($y_{\mathrm{init}} = 9.0238$).
    \item \textbf{Levy 2D}: Dominated by high-frequency oscillatory ridges and deceptive local valleys. Global minimum at $(1, 1)$ with $f(1, 1)=0$. Initialized in the distant corner $[-4.5, -2.5]^2$ ($y_{\mathrm{init}} = 3.9196$).
\end{enumerate}

