\subsection{High-Dimensional Continuous Control and Robotics ($d=32$ and $d=60$)}
To demonstrate scalability where Gaussian Processes suffer from distance concentration, we evaluate on two high-dimensional domains (Table~\ref{tab:high_dim_results}):
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Pendulum-v1 Policy Optimization ($d=32$)}: Direct weight policy search ($\mathbf{x} \in [-2, 2]^{32}$) for nonlinear swing-up. Exact GP-BO stalls at 1033.2 due to kernel flattening, and multi-head DP-BO suffers from variance dilution (1209.1). In contrast, \textbf{Single-Network DP-TS achieves the lowest regret (927.1)}, successfully coordinating swing-up.
    \item \textbf{Rover Trajectory Planning ($d=60$)}: Continuous optimization of 30 2D waypoints in $[0, 1]^{60}$ around 4 circular hazardous obstacles \citep{wang2018batched,eriksson2019scalable}. Initialized from colliding trajectories (cost $6.772$, Figure~\ref{fig:rover_60d}), DP-TS discovers smooth, collision-free detours, reaching the lowest overall cost of \textbf{2.203} in 21.8~ms/step.
\end{enumerate}

